  "scope": "# Review handoff \u2014 4c26a1072222\nTask `4c26a1072222`; reviewed source version `2.1.0`, SHA-256 `5816599d9ed224a6d95f56745292449c464b6e708cac9373db58e8671b8aa22d`; rule hash `a86a18b84011`.\nDefect: three source colors perfectly predicted transpose/anti-transpose membership, so a cue-gated shortcut could avoid learning the A\u2192B relation.\nRepair: every lesson now contains a causally active three-color non-transpose band; the exact cue gate is a declared canonical-fitting competitor with a linked witness.\nReference rule: unchanged; canonical Racket bytes, default semantics, transform selector, dimensions, and palette contract remain fixed.\nFocused verification: 32/32 tests pass; final log `checks/final-focused-tests.log`.\nRacket verification: two forward/inverse prototype episodes, 32/32 executions, exact parity, four demonstrations plus four distinct queries each; `checks/parametric/manifest.json`.\nAdversarial pass: 16 episode cases and 152 unique inputs across seed/count/export/rejection boundaries; `checks/parametric-adversarial.json`.\nSupplementary tickets: allocation-quality and adversarial-witness both completed within one bounded live probe each; evidence under `checks/tickets/`.\nRemaining limits: inverse mode is a prototype only; explicit 512-retry exhaustion was not forced; the allocation sample did not include ARC-GEN or RE-ARC; the optional storage study is missing `before_extract` because extraction had already occurred, and it was not reconstructed.\nDisposition: routine source repair with a needs-attention prototype; no catalog approval, production variant wiring, training admission, or peer safety finding is claimed.\n",
